From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:09:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/79] flashnext_mia: her settings through
 platform/environment.zig

Every setting her engine reads (57 names, TF_FLASHNEXT_* plus
TF_TP_TIMEOUT_S and TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB) has a row in a new
flashnext_mia scope, checked when her engine opens (cuda_env.startup), as
the DeepSeek rows are. Her readers keep interpreting the text, so every
accepted value keeps its meaning; the rows refuse only text they misread.
The table gains a list kind (comma-separated words or whole numbers) and
off words for a real row (TF_FLASHNEXT_YARN's). Names and meanings are
unchanged; CONFIDENCE and KEEP_LATE keep hers under TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia.
docs/environment.md lists them. TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE joins the environment
test's covered rows.
